From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz <dariusz@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:08:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] linuxcnc: clear G76 passes safely on Stop and Step

Give each generated G76 pass an internal identity spanning its safe approach, synchronized cut, and exact clearance retract. Stop latches the active pass and finishes only its marked retract, including when the target arrives after the cut or the request crosses the cut/retract handoff.

Split Single Step into two internal units per pass: return to the pass start while remaining at safe clearance, followed by the infeed, synchronized thread, and clearance retract together. Teach motion-level Step to preserve those same boundaries when later passes were already queued by AUTO_RUN, while ordinary unmarked motion retains source-line stepping.

Preserve pass ownership on synthetic blend arcs, make marked clearance endpoints non-blendable, reset pass-step state on abort and mode changes, and extend resumable-stop coverage to cylindrical and tapered Stop-to-Step handoffs, exit tapers, arc blending, deterministic cut/retract timing, and two-step safe-approach/thread-clearance sequencing.
