diff --git a/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc b/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc
index 4160cfb4a2..760cfe2384 100644
--- a/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc
@@ -1986,6 +1986,21 @@ pass, so a relief groove will be required at the entry unless the
 beginning of the thread is past the end of the material or an entry
 taper is used.
 
+In Single Step mode, each G76 pass is two steps. The first step moves to the
+pass start while remaining at the safe clearance depth. The second step
+performs the infeed, synchronized cut, and immediate retract to the pass
+clearance position. The next step begins the next pass. These internal fences
+do not drain the motion queue during normal, uninterrupted `AUTO_RUN`
+execution. The safe approach endpoint and marked clearance retract are exact,
+non-blendable endpoints while stepping, so motion reaches zero velocity at
+both boundaries.
+
+When resumable Stop is enabled, a Stop requested during a G76 cut or its
+immediate clearance retract completes that explicitly marked retract before
+stopping. A later rapid outside the G76 pass is not part of this safe boundary.
+If later passes were already queued by `AUTO_RUN`, subsequent Single Steps
+still alternate between one approach and its synchronized cut plus clearance.
+
 Unless using an exit taper, the exit move is not synchronized to the
 spindle speed and will be a <<gcode:g0,rapid move>>. With a slow spindle,
 the exit move might take only a small fraction of a revolution. If the
