diff --git a/tests/resumable-stop/README b/tests/resumable-stop/README
index e457195324..e845030ffb 100644
--- a/tests/resumable-stop/README
+++ b/tests/resumable-stop/README
@@ -5,6 +5,22 @@ This regression test exercises the task-level Stop operation directly through
 the Python command API. It checks that an active feed move stops without
 aborting queued AUTO state, that spindle and coolant outputs are disabled
 while stopped, and that Resume restores them before continuing the same
-program to completion. The G95 scenario enables the jerk-limited trajectory
-planner and rejects zero-limit Ruckig fallback errors while spindle feedback
-recovers after Resume.
+program to completion. The G76 scenarios check that Stop executes only the
+explicitly marked post-cut rapid retract, leaving the tool clear of the
+finished thread rather than stopped at cutting depth. Coverage includes
+cylindrical and tapered drive lines, synchronized exit tapers, repeated Stop
+requests across the cut/retract handoff, and a negative G33 test proving that
+an unrelated following rapid is not executed. Single Step coverage enters the
+first G76 pass directly and verifies every cylindrical and tapered safe
+approach step followed by its combined infeed, synchronized-cut, and clearance
+step. It also starts G76 in normal AUTO_RUN, stops after the first pass with later passes
+already queued, and verifies that each
+following AUTO_STEP reaches exactly one cylindrical or tapered safe approach
+endpoint, and the next AUTO_STEP completes that pass's infeed, thread, and
+clearance.
+Arc blending is enabled for all scenarios, so the exact-clearance assertions
+also prove that a marked G76 retract endpoint is not trimmed by a following
+rapid. The handoff stress case uses a slow synchronized feed and issues Stop at
+least 20 task cycles before the cut endpoint. The G95 scenario enables the
+jerk-limited trajectory planner and rejects zero-limit Ruckig fallback errors
+while spindle feedback recovers after Resume.
